{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And they went down, etc., into the pit (she'olah).</b> Meaning, that the earth did not have dominion over them to kill them, but they remained alive, and the earth was given as a deposit for Gehinnom. And this is what it says — <b>alive into the pit (she'olah)</b> — and it does not say 'to Sheol.' And although every word that requires a prefix-letter (letter of measure) at its beginning has the letter heh appended at its end, <b>nevertheless</b> this is not done for nothing, and the intention is that after they descended to Sheol, HaShem gave them strength and they did not die — on the path of their statement, of blessed memory (Sanhedrin 110a), that the Holy One, blessed be He, gives strength to the wicked to receive their punishment. So too these remained alive after they were in Sheol itself, in order to intensify their sensation. And if it had said 'to Sheol,' it would have been understood that they were alive only until their arrival at Sheol, and upon arriving they died and had no vitality after they reached Sheol."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:30.750634114Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}